    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup today is headlined by the elite potential of **Gunnar Henderson** (81.00) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66), both of whom benefit significantly from facing Cade Cavalli and Chris Bassitt, respectively. **Gunnar Henderson** is the clear anchor, leveraging a high-ceiling matchup against a middling arm with a 14% boost from a favorable platoon split and the premier leadoff spot. Meanwhile, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** has emerged as a high-value play today, with a 14% dynamic platoon edge driving his score into the 70s. We are also leaning into the high-upside profiles of **Heliot Ramos** (65.50) and **Sam Antonacci** (63.68); **Heliot Ramos** benefits from a massive 10% park factor bump, while **Sam Antonacci** carries an elite 0.402 xwOBA that makes him a must-start despite his opponent\u2019s SP efficiency.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the rotation today involved the exclusion of **Josh Jung**, who narrowly missed the cut with a 48.45 score. While **Josh Jung** offered solid baseline expectations, his lack of high-leverage situational multipliers\u2014specifically the absence of elite SB upside\u2014kept him below our current threshold compared to the dynamic platoon edges offered by **Brady House** and **Miguel Vargas**. We are also exercising caution with **Jackson Merrill** (52.77) and **Andy Pages** (55.44); **Jackson Merrill** faces the toughest test of the day in Logan Gilbert, where a significant SP skill penalty (\u201319%) drags down his efficiency, and **Andy Pages** is navigating a slight headwind in the catcher-controlled base-stealing department. All starters are currently flagged under \"Lineup Pending\" status, so we must monitor for late substitutions that could alter these platoon and order-based projections before first pitch.",
